{
 "id": "rewrite/break-then-payback-turns/hot/5m",
 "description": "coref reduces a 20,000-token output (message 1) inside the cached prefix with 20,000 tokens after it. Request 1 saves 19,900 x $0.30 = +$0.00597 and breaks 20,100 tokens, 20,100 x $3.45 = -$0.06935: net -$0.06338. Each of the next 11 hot requests saves +$0.00597. The cumulative net is still -$0.00368 after 10 replays and turns positive on the 11th (+$0.00230). A cold request 25 minutes later saves 19,900 x $3.75 = +$0.07463, because the content would have been written.",
 "source": "issue_cases.md#232",
 "dims": {
  "kind": "rewrite",
  "position": "beforeBStar",
  "cache": "break-then-hits-then-miss",
  "ttl": "5m",
  "lifetime": "exact",
  "break": "plugin",
  "replay": "true"
 },
 "rates": "fixture-v1",
 "open": [
  "design \u00a75.1 snaps B* to the last client breakpoint at or before the previous body's end, and the client's breakpoints are the current request's own: system and the new last message. Read literally that gives the end of system, not the end of the previous body. The examples, and this case, take the end of the previous body."
 ],
